  data: {
    LLM: "As a game of 100% chance, there is no active strategy. However, the '6 beats Ace' mechanic means that your deck's health is cyclical. If you have many 6s, you are effectively protected against an opponent with many Aces.\n\nThe 'Bottom-Loading' Effect: In physical play, the order in which you pick up the tricks and place them at the bottom of your deck matters. Savvy players try to sandwich high cards between lower cards to avoid 'Dispute' clusters later in the game.\n\nStamina Tracking: In long games, players begin to memorize the 'Loop' of their cards. If you know a cluster of Jacks is coming up, you can predict when you might enter a Dispute round.",
    Player: "As a game of 100% chance, there is no active strategy. However, the '6 beats Ace' mechanic means that your deck's health is cyclical. If you have many 6s, you are effectively protected against an opponent with many Aces.\n\nThe 'Bottom-Loading' Effect: In physical play, the order in which you pick up the tricks and place them at the bottom of your deck matters. Savvy players try to sandwich high cards between lower cards to avoid 'Dispute' clusters later in the game.\n\nStamina Tracking: In long games, players begin to memorize the 'Loop' of their cards. If you know a cluster of Jacks is coming up, you can predict when you might enter a Dispute round.",
